Multicontainer

need compose.yaml file in the root folder to create a multicontainer app.

services:
  app1:
    build:
      context: ./app
    depends_on:
      - db1
    environment:
      NODE_ENV: production
    ports:
      - 3000:3000
      - 35729:35729
    develop:
      watch:
        - path: ./app/package.json
          action: rebuild
        - path: ./app
          target: /usr/src/app
          action: sync

  db1:
    image: mongo:6
    volumes: 
      - database:/data/db
    ports:
      - 27017:27017


 then run docker compose up -d           
 -> This command builds and runs all the services listed in the compose file in a detached mode.



 docker compose watch                  
 ->When developing with Docker, you may need to automatically update and preview your running services as you edit and save your code. We use docker compose watch for this.



you can run below cmd anytime to resume your app evenif you delete the image. it will simply get back from compose file
docker compose up 
